    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe new `CapMembershipLevel` class itself is clean and idiomatic \u2014 it mirrors `CountHouseholdMembers` almost exactly (same `service(@Val Owner, OwnerRepository)` shape, same `findAll().stream()` filter chain on id/`deleted`/`household::matches`, reuses `HouseholdKey`), has a clear javadoc, and is wired into the pipeline in the natural spot right after `assignMembershipLevel`. The *addition* is well-formed.\n\nThe problem is what the diff silently *removes*, which has nothing to do with the spec:\n\n1. **Unrelated deletion of the `rejectDuplicateIdentity` step.** The YAML diff drops the entire `rejectDuplicateIdentity` step (and its explanatory comment) from `owners.POST.yml`. The spec is only about capping `membershipLevel`; there is no reason the cap change should touch the household 409 duplicate-identity block, which lives in a completely different part of the pipeline. This change is not additive \u2014 it strips an existing feature (409 rejection of a second owner in an occupied household, including the `sharesHousehold` bypass).\n\n2. **Orphaned classes left behind.** As a result of (1), `RejectDuplicateIdentity.java`, `DuplicateIdentityException.java`, `DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler.java`, and `escalation/...DuplicateIdentityException.yml` are now dead/unwired \u2014 the POST pipeline was their only caller. A maintainer would be surprised to find a whole exception + handler + function class with no reachable reference, and would not find this coherent.\n\nRecommended fix: restore the `rejectDuplicateIdentity` step in `owners.POST.yml` (re-link `assignHousehold.next: rejectDuplicateIdentity` \u2192 `rejectCityAtCapacity`), keeping the `capMembershipLevel` insertion as the only change this diff makes.\n\nMinor (not blocking): in `CapMembershipLevel`, `java.util.Objects::nonNull` is referenced fully-qualified inline while `OptionalInt` is imported at the top \u2014 add a normal `import java.util.Objects;` to match the file's import style.",
